From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 06:33:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] lite: link abseil's log and check libraries

TFLite's own sources use abseil's logging (absl/log/log.h and
absl/log/check.h in core, kernels and delegates), but tensorflow-lite only
links absl::flags, hash, status, strings, synchronization and variant. Built
as a shared library against a shared abseil, libtensorflow-lite.so is then
left with undefined references to absl::log_internal::LogMessage and the
nullguard symbols and no DT_NEEDED entry for the libraries that define them.
Linking an executable against it then fails, since ld does not allow
undefined symbols in the shared libraries of an executable by default, unless
the executable names those abseil libraries itself.

Link absl::log and absl::check as well, so the library records what it
needs.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
diff --git a/tensorflow/lite/CMakeLists.txt b/tensorflow/lite/CMakeLists.txt
index 80c5ae0..79eeba0 100644
--- a/tensorflow/lite/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/tensorflow/lite/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -759,8 +759,10 @@ target_include_directories(tensorflow-lite
 target_link_libraries(tensorflow-lite
   PUBLIC
     Eigen3::Eigen
+    absl::check
     absl::flags
     absl::hash
+    absl::log
     absl::status
     absl::strings
     absl::synchronization
